Pandas — Tables and Data Analysis 📊

Pandas is mainly used to work with structured/tabular data.

For example, an Excel-like table:

Name     Age    Salary
John     25     30000
Mary     30     40000
Bill     28     35000

====

Python:

import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Name": ["John", "Mary", "Bill"],
    "Age": [25, 30, 28],
    "Salary": [30000, 40000, 35000]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print(df)

Now you can easily:

df["Salary"].mean()

Filter:

df[df["Salary"] > 30000]

Sort:

df.sort_values("Salary")
Think:

Pandas = Excel-like tables + Data Analysis

====
